---
import Navigation from "../components/header/navigation.astro";
import WelcomeVideo from "../components/welcomeVideo/welcome.astro";
import Footer from "../components/footer/footer.astro";
import Arrow from "../assets/media/images/misc/Arrow.png";
import Software from "../assets/media/images/misc/DesktopComputer.png";
import Business from "../assets/media/images/misc/BriefCase.png";
import Mechanical from "../assets/media/images/misc/Gear.png";
import Electrical from "../assets/media/images/misc/Power.png";
import Colab from "../assets/media/images/sponsors/colab.png";
import Pegnl from "../assets/media/images/sponsors/pegnl.svg";
import "../styles/global.css";
import "../styles/index.css";
---

<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.googleapis.com" />
    <link rel="preconnect" href="https://fonts.gstatic.com" crossorigin />
    <link
      href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=IBM+Plex+Mono:ital,wght@0,100;0,200;0,300;0,400;0,500;0,600;0,700;1,100;1,200;1,300;1,400;1,500;1,600;1,700&display=swap"
      rel="stylesheet"
    />
    <link
      rel="icon"
      type="image/png"
      href="/favicon/favicon-96x96.png"
      sizes="96x96"
    />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width" />
    <meta name="generator" content={Astro.generator} />
    <title>Sidus Robotics</title>
    <script src="../components/scripts/countdown.js"></script>
    <script src="../components/scripts/lazyload.js"></script>
  </head>

  <body>
    <Navigation />
    <WelcomeVideo/>

    <section class="content-container" id="index-main-content">
      <div class="content" id="summary">
        <h1>WHO WE ARE</h1>
        <p>
          Sidus Robotics is Memorial University's first-ever Mars rover design
          team, comprised of a diverse group of students from engineering,
          computer science, and business. We are preparing to compete in the
          2026 Canadian International Rover Challenge (CIRC), where university
          teams design and build a rover capable of operating in Mars-like
          conditions. By taking on this challenge, Sidus Robotics not only
          provides members with invaluable real-world experience but also puts
          Newfoundland and Memorial University on the national stage in space
          robotics and engineering.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="content-container" id="index-secondary-content">
      <div class="container">
        <h1>SUBTEAMS</h1>
      </div>

      <div class="content" id="sub-teams">
        <div class="info-blocks" id="mechanical-block">
          <h3>MECHANICAL</h3>
          <div class="blur-load">
            <!-- <img loading="lazy" src={Mechanical.src} alt="gear.png" /> -->
          </div>
          <p>
            From the rigidity of the chassis and suspension to the complexity of
            the arm, the mechanical team is responsible for ensuring the designs
            meet competition specifications and uphold the teams standard of
            functionality by using CAD software, practical experience, and
            course knowledge.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="info-blocks" id="software-block">
          <h3>SOFTWARE</h3>
          <div class="blur-load">
            <!-- <img
              loading="lazy"
              src={Software.src}
              alt=""
              class="bigger-icon-fix"
            /> -->
          </div>
          <p>
            The software team is responsible for designing and developing the
            software that controls the rover. This includes integrating the
            rover's control systems and sensors with the onboard computer, as
            well as creating a graphical user interface on the base station for
            real-time control and sensor data visualization. In the future, the
            team will expand its focus to developing AI that enables the rover
            to operate autonomously and complete tasks without human
            intervention.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="info-blocks" id="electrical-block">
          <h3>ELECTRICAL</h3>
          <div class="blur-load">
            <!-- <img loading="lazy" src={Electrical.src} alt="" /> -->
          </div>
          <p>
            Our electrical team carries out many critical jobs within the rover.
            Proper power distribution circuitry for supplying voltage and power
            levels to all circuits within the rover. Moreover, wireless
            communications and sensors used for navigation and control. The
            electrical team carries out these responsibilities to optimize
            system performance in order to carry out operations effectively and
            reliably.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="info-blocks" id="business-block">
          <h3>BUSINESS</h3>
          <div class="blur-load">
            <!-- <img loading="lazy" src={Business.src} alt="briefcase.png" /> -->
          </div>
          <p>
            The Business Team drives our mission forward by managing finances,
            securing sponsorships, and handling marketing. Just like our rover
            navigates challenges, we strategize to secure resources and maintain
            a strong public presence.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
    
    <section class="content-container" id="index-tertiary-content">
      <div class="container">
        <h1>SPONSORS</h1>
        <h1 class="" id="bronze-medal">BRONZE</h1>
      </div>

      <!-- <div class="image-block">
        <div class="blur-load">
          <a href="https://www.colabsoftware.com/"
            ><img
              loading="lazy"
              src={Colab.src}
              alt="colab.png"
              id="colab"
            /></a
          >
          <a href="https://pegnl.ca/"
            ><img
              loading="lazy"
              src={Pegnl.src}
              alt="pegnl.svg"
              id="pegnl"
            /></a
          >
        </div>
      </div> -->
    </section>
    <Footer />
  </body>
</html>
